<main class="container">
  <h1 style="margin:18px 0 4px;font-size:32px;letter-spacing:-0.03em">Limits and glossary</h1>
  <p class="muted">A short list of what this observatory does not do, followed by the terms needed to read it.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>What it does not say</h2></div>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>It does not predict the result.</strong> It is an average of published polls, not a forecast or a seat projection.</li>
      <li><strong>It does not estimate voting intention.</strong> It aggregates what polling houses publish.</li>
      <li><strong>The range is not a confidence interval.</strong> It is the observed min–max among the polls included.</li>
      <li><strong>It does not correct for demographics.</strong> It does not model age, sex, income or territory.</li>
      <li><strong>The hemicycle is not the Congress.</strong> It uses a national district and excludes regional parties.</li>
      <li><strong>It does not attribute coordination or campaigns.</strong> It measures published polls, not actors’ intentions.</li>
      <li><strong>It does not publish polls during the blackout.</strong> From 24 to 28 November 2026 the data and OG files are withdrawn and the endpoints return 410.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>Key terms</h2></div>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Poll average:</strong> weighted mean of published polls in a window. Not a single survey.</li>
      <li><strong>Range:</strong> minimum and maximum observed. Sensitive to a single outlier.</li>
      <li><strong>IQR:</strong> interquartile range; the middle 50% of the polls. More robust than min–max.</li>
      <li><strong>House effect:</strong> the difference between a pollster’s latest result and the average. Not a bias score.</li>
      <li><strong>Source vs house:</strong> a source is where the poll was captured; a house is the pollster. One source can compile several houses; they are not added.</li>
      <li><strong>D’Hondt:</strong> the seat allocation method used in Spain. The hemicycle applies it nationally as a mechanical exercise.</li>
      <li><strong>Closed and blocked list:</strong> voters choose a party list, not the order of its members (Congress).</li>
      <li><strong>Blackout:</strong> the legal period when polls cannot be published, disseminated or reproduced (24–28 November 2026).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

